WEBVTT

00:01.120 --> 00:04.800
[theme song playing]

00:04.880 --> 00:06.280
[goat bleating]

00:15.240 --> 00:17.080
[people chattering]

00:34.600 --> 00:36.640
[woman screaming with pleasure]

00:41.600 --> 00:43.120
Would you stop the noise?

00:45.320 --> 00:47.960
[Campbell moaning and gasping]

01:04.840 --> 01:06.680
[sniffing]

01:08.280 --> 01:09.640
You're working tonight?

01:09.800 --> 01:11.200
[chuckles]

01:11.320 --> 01:13.840
Not so much work as pleasure.

01:13.960 --> 01:17.080
Others are doing my work
for me tonight.

01:17.240 --> 01:20.400
Gentlemen, welcome, welcome.

01:20.520 --> 01:23.160
- [Arthur] Mr. Solomons.
- You must be Arthur.

01:23.240 --> 01:24.840
- That is right.
- Arthur,

01:24.920 --> 01:27.240
- Arthur!
- A pleasure to meet you, sir.

01:27.320 --> 01:29.200
I've heard so much about you.

01:29.280 --> 01:31.760
Shalom, let me just say.

01:33.000 --> 01:34.160
Shalom.

01:36.560 --> 01:38.200
[plate breaks]

01:38.280 --> 01:39.560
For luck.

01:41.000 --> 01:42.800
[cocks gun]

01:42.960 --> 01:46.040
[theme music continues]

01:57.880 --> 02:01.080
You know, I'm the commanding officer
on this operation?

02:01.160 --> 02:03.160
You are here
purely as an observer.

02:05.600 --> 02:06.840
Just do your duty.

02:09.120 --> 02:10.360
[Polly] Dear Lord,

02:11.240 --> 02:13.200
for what we are
about to receive,

02:13.280 --> 02:15.360
may the Lord make us
truly grateful.

02:15.560 --> 02:16.680
Amen.

02:20.720 --> 02:21.920
Amen.

02:23.600 --> 02:24.760
Amen.

02:27.320 --> 02:30.920
The Passover started off
way out there in the Far East,

02:31.000 --> 02:34.920
out in the sand, out in the desert,
where my forefathers come from.

02:35.000 --> 02:37.560
The Jews, the brews,
whatever you call them.

02:37.640 --> 02:39.880
[bang]
...a little speck on the horizon

02:39.960 --> 02:42.080
- Arthur, this ain't right!
- Billy.

02:42.160 --> 02:44.080
Billy, if you want
you can leave.

02:44.160 --> 02:47.560
If you need to go to the little
boy's room, you can leave.

02:47.640 --> 02:49.200
He's all right. Billy boy.

02:49.320 --> 02:51.880
- Do you want to leave?
- No, I'm all right.

02:51.960 --> 02:53.800
- You want to stay?
- I'll stay.

02:53.880 --> 02:56.160
You stay there, then, treacle. Okay.

02:56.240 --> 02:59.560
So, the Pharaoh,
have you heard of him?

02:59.640 --> 03:03.120
He kept my people,
the Jewish people, in slavery

03:03.200 --> 03:05.800
for thousands and thousands of years.

03:05.880 --> 03:07.520
Persecuted race.

03:07.600 --> 03:10.680
He did, he persecuted my race.

03:10.760 --> 03:13.000
The killing of the innocent, right?

03:13.080 --> 03:16.160
Seder, this feast that what
we is having here, right?

03:16.240 --> 03:18.760
Seder is basically the day

03:18.840 --> 03:22.680
what when the Jewish angels
decided, you know,

03:22.760 --> 03:26.640
that the evil fucking Egyptians
had pushed their fucking luck.

03:26.720 --> 03:27.720
[Arthur] Right.

03:27.800 --> 03:31.160
It's part of our tradition
to do with Seder, right,

03:31.240 --> 03:36.200
that in order to make it good
with God to kill a king,

03:37.760 --> 03:41.280
we have to carry out
the Korban Pesach.

03:41.360 --> 03:45.560
- Right.
- That is the ritual sacrifice

03:45.640 --> 03:47.640
of the Passover goat.

03:48.840 --> 03:50.040
[goat bleats]

03:52.480 --> 03:53.760
It's a goat!

03:53.840 --> 03:56.080
Yeah, and we are going
to sacrifice it.

03:56.960 --> 03:58.200
Tonight.

03:59.080 --> 04:02.800
That's part of the reason why
we have to shut the doors as well.

04:02.880 --> 04:06.600
But this year we thought that
we'd give the fucking goat a name.

04:06.680 --> 04:09.120
- You've named it?
- We fucking did. Yeah.

04:09.200 --> 04:13.000
- They named the goat.
- After the evil fucking Egyptian pharaoh.

04:13.080 --> 04:15.160
- The fucking enemy!
- That's right!

04:15.240 --> 04:16.840
You know what
we called him?

04:16.920 --> 04:19.280
- What did you call him?
- Tommy Shelby.

04:19.720 --> 04:21.320
[shouting]

04:22.160 --> 04:23.760
[Arthur grunting]

04:24.000 --> 04:25.240
Fuck!

04:33.240 --> 04:35.520
[guns cocking]

04:35.600 --> 04:38.680
- [door opens loudly]
- Police! Stay where you are.

04:38.760 --> 04:39.920
[police shouting]

04:40.720 --> 04:42.800
[shoots gun]

04:42.880 --> 04:43.960
You're all fired.

04:44.040 --> 04:45.440
- Eh?
- Fuck you!

04:45.520 --> 04:46.560
[grunts]

04:46.640 --> 04:48.840
That's right,
let's take the load off.

04:51.000 --> 04:52.080
So...

04:53.280 --> 04:56.080
Then the evil Egyptian scum

04:56.720 --> 04:58.800
was finally cleansed

04:58.880 --> 05:01.880
by the blood
of the Passover goat.

05:03.000 --> 05:04.040
[grunts]

05:04.120 --> 05:08.760
[breathing heavily]

05:09.720 --> 05:11.560
That's from Sabini.

05:12.800 --> 05:15.040
[Sabini] You tell your Gypsy king...

05:15.120 --> 05:18.040
[screams]
...that whoever comes down south

05:18.120 --> 05:22.520
shall return north
in many fucking pieces.

05:22.880 --> 05:24.160
Huh?

05:25.800 --> 05:26.840
[screams]

05:26.920 --> 05:28.040
[gunshot]

05:37.120 --> 05:39.680
[Solomons] The fucking animal.
came in here,

05:39.760 --> 05:42.880
with a gun and a razor,
he shot him in the face.

05:42.960 --> 05:46.200
My lads, they restrained him.
Look at him. He is dead.

05:46.280 --> 05:47.560
Is he dead?

05:47.880 --> 05:49.320
He is fucking dead!

05:49.400 --> 05:52.800
He want arresting
or something, right? Surely.

05:58.520 --> 06:02.800
[Polly] Not again! Michael! No,
you can't take my son away again! 

06:02.880 --> 06:05.240
- Give me the boy.
- Come back here.

06:05.320 --> 06:08.240
We are arresting him
for taking part in a fight...

06:08.320 --> 06:10.360
[Polly shouts]
[grunts in pain]

06:10.440 --> 06:12.360
Don't you fucking touch him!

06:12.440 --> 06:13.680
Get off him!

06:13.760 --> 06:14.880
Don't say anything.

06:14.960 --> 06:16.320
Tommy will get you out.

06:16.400 --> 06:17.560
I'll be all right--

06:18.520 --> 06:19.800
[short scream]

06:23.200 --> 06:26.400
You should know
that as of this night,

06:26.480 --> 06:28.480
Tommy Shelby is finished.

06:42.400 --> 06:46.120
Mick, this is Thomas Shelby.
He's come to check up on his filly.

06:47.680 --> 06:49.240
Yes. I've heard about him.

06:50.560 --> 06:53.120
[May] Micky is the best
horseman in England.

06:54.880 --> 06:57.080
He likes to waste money,
I know that.

06:57.160 --> 06:58.640
According to the reports

06:58.760 --> 07:01.760
you're spending two pound
a month on worming powder.

07:01.840 --> 07:06.040
- You want a horse with worms?
- Horses get worms from the water trough.

07:06.160 --> 07:08.680
If you put goldfish,
they eat the worm eggs.

07:08.800 --> 07:10.080
Goldfish?

07:10.360 --> 07:14.240
- That'll be a Gypsy thing, is it?
- No, it's an accounting thing.

07:15.000 --> 07:16.640
Goldfish cost a penny each.

07:16.720 --> 07:18.600
Or you can win them at the fair.

07:22.080 --> 07:25.680
If you want, I'll dispense with
the vet altogether. Excuse me.

07:29.240 --> 07:31.680
You ever consider
a career in diplomacy?

07:36.320 --> 07:38.880
Hello, hello. How are you, eh?

07:39.080 --> 07:40.520
Goldfish? Seriously?

07:40.600 --> 07:44.000
Yep. You people have a lot to learn.

08:02.080 --> 08:05.640
They asked me if I wanted a fire
in the guest bedroom.

08:08.080 --> 08:09.440
I said no.

08:11.440 --> 08:12.920
Just one fire tonight.

08:14.760 --> 08:16.480
Bold and fearless, eh?

08:16.800 --> 08:17.800
Yes.

08:19.600 --> 08:21.480
Though I'm not really fearless.

08:27.240 --> 08:28.600
[door opens]

08:30.720 --> 08:32.760
- [Thomas] Drink?
- [May] Why not?

08:46.160 --> 08:50.280
- Madam, there is a telephone call.
- I'll take it in the drawing room.

08:50.360 --> 08:51.840
It's for Mr. Shelby.

08:53.840 --> 08:55.720
[door opens]

08:55.800 --> 08:56.920
We had a deal.

08:58.280 --> 08:59.480
Hey!

09:00.160 --> 09:02.000
We had a fucking deal!

09:02.480 --> 09:06.520
I would think you would moderate
your language in a place of worship.

09:07.880 --> 09:10.000
We had a fucking deal.

09:13.240 --> 09:14.520
Mr. Shelby.

09:16.680 --> 09:19.360
If you read the papers,

09:19.440 --> 09:21.920
you might have seen
that the Home Secretary

09:22.000 --> 09:24.360
has got himself into a bit of a fizz

09:24.440 --> 09:27.040
about certain moral issues.

09:27.360 --> 09:29.640
Prostitution, protection,

09:29.720 --> 09:32.760
racketeering, drinking,
cocaine and, of course...

09:33.880 --> 09:35.040
Gambling.

09:35.920 --> 09:37.640
And he has demanded results.

09:37.760 --> 09:40.280
You offered me protection.

09:40.360 --> 09:42.760
You promised me protection.

09:42.840 --> 09:45.800
Well, no, you see,
it was Mr. Churchill

09:45.880 --> 09:47.640
that made you that promise.

09:48.480 --> 09:52.040
And the Home Secretary
outranks him, so...

09:54.120 --> 09:56.880
And I cannot be blamed
if your demented brother

09:56.960 --> 10:00.160
decides to go on some sort of
blood orgy during dinner.

10:00.240 --> 10:01.480
Don't you lie to me!

10:01.560 --> 10:05.200
Do not sit here in your fucking church
and lie to me!

10:06.880 --> 10:11.480
You will need to contain your emotions
or this meeting is at an end.

10:20.600 --> 10:21.600
Good.

10:23.680 --> 10:24.880
That's better.

10:27.200 --> 10:28.360
So...

10:29.520 --> 10:33.200
Let us review the new situation.

10:33.280 --> 10:35.680
I have your brother
in a prison cell,

10:35.760 --> 10:38.160
charged with the murder
of Billy Kitchen.

10:39.040 --> 10:41.120
The case against him is strong

10:41.760 --> 10:45.400
and I have no doubt
that his destiny is to hang.

10:46.080 --> 10:48.560
And then there is
Polly's son, Michael.

10:48.800 --> 10:50.960
He has already admitted to helping

10:51.040 --> 10:53.720
Arthur burn down the Marquis pub.

10:54.960 --> 10:56.040
Oh!

10:56.120 --> 10:59.520
He was a tough nut to crack,
that boy, but crack he did.

10:59.920 --> 11:02.320
So, I have your brother
facing the noose,

11:02.400 --> 11:05.120
I have your cousin
facing five years for arson.

11:05.200 --> 11:08.120
And I have your entire

11:08.200 --> 11:11.680
organization in disarray
in Birmingham and in London.

11:11.760 --> 11:13.040
What do you want?

11:13.960 --> 11:15.200
What do I want?

11:16.480 --> 11:17.920
I don't understand.

11:19.720 --> 11:21.200
I have already agreed

11:21.320 --> 11:23.400
to do your fucking killing for you.

11:24.720 --> 11:25.960
Now, what is it

11:26.040 --> 11:28.280
you want from me?

11:28.360 --> 11:31.600
Oh. There you go. You see...

11:33.760 --> 11:38.320
An agreement is not the same thing
as an assurance, now, is it?

11:39.720 --> 11:42.160
You see, I found...

11:43.000 --> 11:45.080
I wasn't sleeping so well.

11:46.560 --> 11:48.720
It wasn't just the smell

11:48.800 --> 11:51.000
and the noise in that room, no.

11:51.960 --> 11:53.920
It was the nagging doubt.

11:54.000 --> 11:55.320
The knowledge...

11:56.040 --> 11:57.680
The knowledge that...

11:59.240 --> 12:02.240
Tommy Shelby
is not afraid to die.

12:04.280 --> 12:05.720
And therefore,

12:06.760 --> 12:09.720
the threat to your own life
might not be enough

12:10.320 --> 12:11.680
to make it certain that

12:11.760 --> 12:14.960
you will obey me on the given day.

12:16.920 --> 12:19.120
I needed also the power of life

12:19.200 --> 12:21.840
and death over your family.

12:21.920 --> 12:24.400
And that I now have.

12:24.480 --> 12:26.880
Your brother, your cousin...

12:27.520 --> 12:29.000
And your sister.

12:30.360 --> 12:32.960
I have known her address
in Primrose Hill

12:33.040 --> 12:35.120
since the day she moved in.

12:35.840 --> 12:37.720
Now she is safe

12:37.800 --> 12:40.200
only as long as I want her to be.

12:40.440 --> 12:42.120
I've been ahead of you...

12:43.640 --> 12:45.440
Every step of the way.

12:46.320 --> 12:49.320
And, as my father used to say,

12:50.440 --> 12:52.560
to make sure your dog obeys you,

12:52.640 --> 12:55.960
you have to show it the stick
once in a while.

13:00.840 --> 13:02.680
[phone ringing]

13:04.040 --> 13:06.560
Tommy, Arthur
is in solitary confinement.

13:06.640 --> 13:08.520
Michael is in the remand wing--

13:08.640 --> 13:10.800
Yeah. I know.
Get out, shut the doors.

13:13.040 --> 13:15.640
[phone continues ringing]

13:24.920 --> 13:26.400
[Grace] Tommy?

13:27.800 --> 13:28.840
It's me.

13:32.400 --> 13:33.760
Tommy, can you hear me?

13:34.880 --> 13:36.680
Yes, Grace.

13:37.160 --> 13:40.680
I think you called.
I... haven't slept.

13:43.400 --> 13:45.480
Grace, this is not a good time.

13:46.000 --> 13:47.320
I can call you back.

13:47.400 --> 13:50.160
- No, it's fine. It's all right.
- Can we meet?

13:51.440 --> 13:53.440
Yes. We'll meet.

13:54.760 --> 13:55.960
When?

13:59.040 --> 14:01.840
Grace, there are some things
I have to do first.

14:04.680 --> 14:06.200
[door opens]

14:06.280 --> 14:07.760
[door slams shut]

14:07.840 --> 14:09.640
[footsteps approaching]

14:11.160 --> 14:12.240
John?

14:12.960 --> 14:16.080
The coppers have lifted
ten of our men in Camden Town,

14:16.160 --> 14:19.160
- the rest are on the run.
- They've taken Michael.

14:19.240 --> 14:21.520
- Business first.
- They took Michael--

14:21.600 --> 14:24.320
- They picked him up--
- Polly, business first!

14:24.800 --> 14:26.000
John?

14:26.080 --> 14:27.640
They took all our whiskey,

14:28.320 --> 14:30.760
so they'll be sipping that for Christmas.

14:31.080 --> 14:33.280
They've impounded all our vans,

14:33.360 --> 14:35.560
put their own locks on the warehouse.

14:36.760 --> 14:40.800
The Eden club and all our pubs
have been raided by the coppers

14:40.880 --> 14:43.160
and handed back to
Sabini and Solomons.

14:45.120 --> 14:48.320
The Black Country boys think
it was Arthur killed Billy

14:48.400 --> 14:50.800
'cause that's what
the coppers told them.

14:50.920 --> 14:53.560
So no more free passes
for our whiskey boats.

14:53.640 --> 14:57.200
I don't care about whiskey.
I don't care about Billy Kitchen.

14:57.280 --> 14:59.520
I want my son out of prison. Now!

14:59.600 --> 15:01.000
I spoke to Johnny Dogs.

15:01.120 --> 15:04.120
- This meeting should just be family.
- I can help.

15:04.200 --> 15:05.640
She is not blood, Tommy!

15:05.720 --> 15:08.160
- Let her speak.
- Or is this a business--

15:08.280 --> 15:09.400
Enough!

15:10.800 --> 15:12.240
Enough, Polly.

15:12.960 --> 15:14.320
Esme?

15:14.600 --> 15:16.960
I spoke to Johnny Dogs.
The Lees are kin.

15:17.040 --> 15:19.560
- The bloody Lees!
- They can give us men!

15:19.640 --> 15:21.560
We don't need
more fucking men!

15:21.640 --> 15:23.880
It's men that have done
the damage!

15:23.960 --> 15:27.440
It is men fighting like cockerels

15:27.520 --> 15:29.880
that have put us here
in the first place.

15:30.320 --> 15:33.120
Esme, we'll take up their offer.
We need men.

15:40.680 --> 15:44.640
If Michael ever gets out of prison,

15:45.200 --> 15:47.960
I am taking him away
from this family.

15:48.040 --> 15:49.240
For good.

15:51.560 --> 15:53.600
This life is bad.

15:57.360 --> 16:00.120
This life is all bad.

16:00.200 --> 16:03.560
- [Finn] Aunt Pol, what are you doing?
- Shut up and walk.

16:05.240 --> 16:06.480
[door opens]

16:07.280 --> 16:08.640
[door closes]

16:11.560 --> 16:12.840
Thomas?

16:14.480 --> 16:17.920
Should I go and speak to Queen Mary Lee
at the Black Patch?

16:22.280 --> 16:23.480
Yes.

16:24.080 --> 16:26.560
She can give us soldiers for a few nights.

16:26.640 --> 16:27.680
Good.

16:30.920 --> 16:32.080
John,

16:32.880 --> 16:34.320
go bring up the car.

16:50.800 --> 16:52.200
[door opens]

16:53.800 --> 16:56.480
- [door closes]
- Imagine riding away, Thomas.

16:57.640 --> 16:59.480
Living the real life, you know?

17:00.720 --> 17:02.640
Your Gypsy half is the stronger.

17:04.960 --> 17:07.080
You just want to ride away.

17:09.160 --> 17:11.560
France is the new place
for us, they say.

17:13.000 --> 17:14.920
Lot of metal lying around still.

17:15.640 --> 17:18.480
Guns and trucks and spent
shells and things.

17:19.800 --> 17:21.000
Then you go south.

17:22.560 --> 17:24.040
Saintes-Maries,

17:24.680 --> 17:26.320
where the Black Madonna is.

17:27.920 --> 17:30.160
My brothers go sometimes
for the fair.

17:32.000 --> 17:33.680
It's like a home for us.

17:37.640 --> 17:39.960
They still let you get lost there.

17:51.720 --> 17:53.800
I've been to France, Esme.

17:55.960 --> 17:57.240
So has John.

17:58.800 --> 18:00.200
Now get your coat

18:01.360 --> 18:02.840
and go with your husband.

18:12.760 --> 18:16.120
If you ever talk about
getting lost again, I'll cut you...

18:17.640 --> 18:19.240
From this family.

18:28.760 --> 18:30.000
What family?

18:46.040 --> 18:47.280
[door lock clanging]

18:49.240 --> 18:51.520
- [knock at door]
- [Campbell] Come in.

18:51.680 --> 18:53.040
[door opens]

18:56.440 --> 18:57.760
Ah.

18:57.840 --> 18:59.000
Polly.

19:00.640 --> 19:02.240
Come to see my son.

19:03.760 --> 19:05.280
Close the door.

19:09.280 --> 19:10.800
I've just been conducting

19:11.520 --> 19:13.080
an interrogation.

19:14.080 --> 19:16.320
It can be awfully hard on the hands.

19:16.880 --> 19:19.120
My son, Michael, where is he?

19:19.680 --> 19:21.680
Do you think I need a shave?

19:23.560 --> 19:25.040
It's been a long day.

19:26.120 --> 19:28.040
I need to shave,
don't you think?

19:29.800 --> 19:33.360
Well, maybe it can wait till later.

19:35.880 --> 19:40.200
Your son has been having
a hard time of it, I am told.

19:40.280 --> 19:43.160
And that is why I thought
that you and I together,

19:43.240 --> 19:46.440
we should do whatever we can
to get him freed.

19:47.560 --> 19:50.560
I have a form here,
a release form,

19:51.480 --> 19:52.960
and with my signature,

19:53.840 --> 19:57.600
he can be freed
by tomorrow morning at dawn.

20:13.760 --> 20:14.880
So sign it.

20:18.200 --> 20:19.560
He didn't do anything.

20:19.640 --> 20:23.320
"Sign it, Mr. Campbell, please, sir."

20:24.680 --> 20:28.160
Something like that, that'd be
a way to say it, wouldn't it?

20:29.440 --> 20:30.520
Now,

20:32.240 --> 20:36.160
what would prompt me
to do you such a favor, hmm?

20:38.400 --> 20:39.440
What do you want?

20:42.680 --> 20:43.720
Information?

20:44.200 --> 20:49.000
You mean inside information about
Tommy Shelby's criminal empire?

20:51.080 --> 20:52.520
With respect,

20:52.880 --> 20:56.600
I would say that I know more
about Tommy's dealings than you do.

20:56.680 --> 21:01.160
He doesn't trouble the family with
Irish business, for instance, does he? No.

21:02.200 --> 21:03.480
So, no.

21:04.920 --> 21:07.200
It's not information I need.

21:14.160 --> 21:16.520
What else could you give me,

21:18.080 --> 21:20.200
in return for my signature?

21:21.720 --> 21:24.480
I'm talking about
a simple transaction here.

21:26.680 --> 21:28.520
I have a great curiosity.

21:30.600 --> 21:33.280
Like the magpie sees something...

21:35.560 --> 21:37.840
Something shining in the mud.

21:39.800 --> 21:42.200
He has no need for the silver...

21:44.000 --> 21:45.840
But he takes it anyway.

21:57.360 --> 21:58.920
[inhales sharply]

22:12.600 --> 22:13.880
Sign the form.

22:14.240 --> 22:15.800
"Please, sir."

22:15.880 --> 22:17.440
Please, sir.

22:20.680 --> 22:23.800
I will sign that form
with this hand,

22:25.400 --> 22:26.840
when I am finished.

22:27.680 --> 22:29.040
It's a deal?

22:29.480 --> 22:30.800
It's a deal.

22:34.840 --> 22:36.200
You don't cry?

22:36.560 --> 22:38.800
- I can cry.
- So...

22:40.720 --> 22:42.480
That is what I want.

22:43.080 --> 22:45.120
I need you to cry.

22:47.040 --> 22:48.480
[shakily] I will try.

22:51.360 --> 22:54.840
"I need a favor,
Mr. Campbell, sir.

22:54.920 --> 22:57.440
And I will do anything...

22:57.520 --> 22:58.840
Anything in return."

22:58.920 --> 23:01.040
That's what
you might have said, hmm?

23:04.320 --> 23:06.240
I felt something when...

23:07.960 --> 23:10.360
When I had you up against that car

23:10.440 --> 23:12.160
and you felt it, too.

23:12.280 --> 23:14.600
Don't tell me you didn't, Polly.

23:14.680 --> 23:16.000
Because--

23:16.760 --> 23:17.920
Oh.

23:18.000 --> 23:19.600
And now you think you're...

23:21.040 --> 23:22.760
So respectable...

23:23.240 --> 23:25.840
With your son and your house

23:25.920 --> 23:28.600
and your maid,
but I know what you are,

23:28.680 --> 23:30.920
you Gypsy Fenian slut.

23:32.640 --> 23:35.960
Do you want it on the floor
or on the desk, Mr. Campbell?

23:46.000 --> 23:47.440
Now you cry.

23:49.040 --> 23:50.560
[loudly] You cry!

23:58.200 --> 24:00.680
Get out. Get out.

24:02.280 --> 24:04.040
Get out!

24:04.120 --> 24:06.160
No. No!

24:06.240 --> 24:07.600
I want him free.

24:08.560 --> 24:09.960
I will get him free.

24:14.280 --> 24:15.720
You don't need to shave.

24:17.800 --> 24:19.600
You don't need to do anything.

24:20.320 --> 24:22.840
[belt buckle jangling]

24:22.920 --> 24:25.560
A victory's just doing
nothing as well.

24:26.520 --> 24:28.240
Doing it soft and gentle.

24:32.240 --> 24:34.040
[breathes raggedly]

24:35.040 --> 24:36.280
[gasps]

24:37.320 --> 24:39.080
Should I talk or not talk?

24:42.440 --> 24:45.680
Should it be like
I am weak and small, yes?

24:48.720 --> 24:50.960
Do you want me to talk
or not to talk?

24:53.200 --> 24:54.360
Talk.

24:54.880 --> 24:56.480
You're small and weak.

24:58.280 --> 25:00.160
Then that is what I am,

25:01.040 --> 25:02.720
small and weak.

25:04.280 --> 25:05.360
Look.

25:07.680 --> 25:08.760
Feel.

25:11.880 --> 25:13.480
You made me cry.

25:17.920 --> 25:19.000
No!

25:20.440 --> 25:22.960
We had an agreement, right?

25:23.040 --> 25:24.880
Yes. Yes!

25:27.120 --> 25:28.800
[door opens]

25:28.880 --> 25:30.680
[door closes]

25:33.520 --> 25:34.800
Where have you been?

25:36.680 --> 25:39.240
I went to the Spotted Dog in Digbeth

25:40.080 --> 25:41.640
for a glass or two of rum.

25:43.440 --> 25:45.160
Was it one glass or two?

25:45.800 --> 25:47.160
It was three.

25:48.320 --> 25:49.560
Where's the baby?

25:50.840 --> 25:52.240
Sleeping.

25:52.880 --> 25:53.920
Hmm?

25:54.000 --> 25:55.320
More like five.

26:00.440 --> 26:01.760
It was more like six.

26:01.840 --> 26:02.960
[chuckles softly]

26:04.480 --> 26:05.800
Did you meet the maid?

26:06.800 --> 26:10.360
I talked politics with her
and she got bored and went to bed.

26:14.440 --> 26:16.440
- I phoned James.
- [chuckling]

26:16.520 --> 26:18.560
He talked to the lawyer anyway.

26:18.640 --> 26:22.280
Said he'd take Arthur's case for free,
so we don't need Tommy.

26:24.760 --> 26:25.800
[exhales heavily]

26:25.880 --> 26:27.080
Pol?

26:28.640 --> 26:31.040
We'll get Michael free as well,
I promise.

26:31.120 --> 26:34.120
There's no need, they'll let him out
in the morning.

26:38.080 --> 26:41.720
If the baby wants anything
at night, ring the bell by the bed.

26:43.200 --> 26:46.840
She gets paid to work 24 hours,
that girl, she's getting lazy.

26:48.400 --> 26:49.560
Well...

26:51.840 --> 26:53.640
Take advantage if you're nice.

27:05.880 --> 27:09.320
[slow song playing]

27:47.040 --> 27:48.360
[lock opening]

28:33.320 --> 28:36.080
You need cream on them cuts
or they'll get bad.

28:43.320 --> 28:45.600
The screws told me
why I've been freed.

28:50.440 --> 28:52.080
They told me what you did.

28:59.160 --> 29:00.720
They thought it was funny.

29:08.080 --> 29:09.280
Maybe it is.

29:17.920 --> 29:19.840
[clanging]

29:34.760 --> 29:36.360
What are you doing, Tommy?

29:37.800 --> 29:39.240
Shoveling shit, Curly.

29:39.840 --> 29:41.480
Just like you.

29:47.960 --> 29:49.440
Why are you doing that?

29:49.520 --> 29:52.280
To remind myself of what I'd be

29:52.360 --> 29:53.760
if I wasn't who I am.

30:25.720 --> 30:27.920
Tommy, what's going on?

30:28.000 --> 30:30.320
I think Tommy's lost his mind, Charlie.

30:32.480 --> 30:35.960
[clears throat]
Well, it's honest work, Curly,

30:37.160 --> 30:39.240
but I don't want to get used to it.

30:40.360 --> 30:43.280
So I'll need six cans of petrol.

30:43.360 --> 30:45.040
Bring them to the garage,

30:46.200 --> 30:48.080
put them in the back of the car.

30:48.720 --> 30:49.960
Six cans?

30:51.240 --> 30:52.600
Tommy,

30:52.680 --> 30:55.800
if you ever want a job,
I'll get you your own shovel.

30:57.200 --> 30:59.160
Petrol, yeah, yeah.

31:15.080 --> 31:19.040
[song playing]

31:51.240 --> 31:53.760
Far too gorgeous
for some half-blind auntie.

31:54.600 --> 31:56.080
She's my harshest critic.

31:56.160 --> 31:57.720
I have to be perfect.

31:59.400 --> 32:01.680
She's not half-blind, she's half-deaf.

32:02.680 --> 32:04.480
So what time will you be back?

32:05.120 --> 32:06.280
Before midnight.

32:08.000 --> 32:09.360
I'll be awake.

32:18.080 --> 32:19.080
Thank you.

33:05.440 --> 33:07.640
- Is this your house?
- Yes.

33:08.560 --> 33:09.680
Have a seat.

33:21.120 --> 33:22.520
Do I not get a drink?

33:23.280 --> 33:24.400
Please.

33:28.600 --> 33:30.800
- You want one?
- Yes.

33:31.000 --> 33:32.120
Still whiskey?

33:33.560 --> 33:34.560
Yes.

33:35.000 --> 33:39.280
But other things have changed.
I saw vans with your name on at the docks.

33:39.360 --> 33:41.280
Yes, some things have changed.

33:59.160 --> 34:01.280
I wasn't sure
about coming tonight--

34:01.360 --> 34:03.520
I lit a fire
in the bedroom upstairs.

34:03.600 --> 34:05.320
[inhales and exhales heavily]

34:05.400 --> 34:07.760
My plan was that we sit here
for a while,

34:09.400 --> 34:12.480
talk about old times,
drink some whiskey.

34:15.640 --> 34:17.320
Then I was gonna tell you...

34:18.000 --> 34:20.760
I hadn't spent a day
without thinking about you.

34:21.520 --> 34:24.680
And then we were gonna
go upstairs and sleep together.

34:26.520 --> 34:28.960
Just now, on the way
to opening the door,

34:30.160 --> 34:31.400
I changed my mind.

34:34.480 --> 34:35.960
So just have one drink,

34:36.040 --> 34:39.400
tell me how happy you are
in New York and then you can go.

34:39.480 --> 34:41.320
- You changed your mind?
- Hmm.

34:42.880 --> 34:45.000
- So you can go.
- Well...

34:48.040 --> 34:51.160
As a matter of fact,
I am happy in New York.

34:51.240 --> 34:54.360
- And I am married.
- Yeah, he's rich, I know.

34:54.440 --> 34:57.280
And he's sweet, and he's kind to me.

34:57.920 --> 35:00.680
So what makes you think that
I'd sleep with you

35:00.760 --> 35:03.080
after one whiskey
and some conversation?

35:03.160 --> 35:06.240
- I was hoping for three whiskeys.
- How dare you?

35:06.520 --> 35:08.800
Doesn't matter now
I've changed my mind.

35:08.880 --> 35:10.800
I came here
because you asked me.

35:10.880 --> 35:13.120
Even though he's sweet
and kind to you?

35:13.200 --> 35:14.880
And now I feel
like an idiot.

35:14.960 --> 35:16.800
- Well, then, go.
- Jesus.

35:28.880 --> 35:30.200
But you're still here.

35:34.760 --> 35:36.320
Are you so certain?

35:36.400 --> 35:38.400
That you're still
in love with me?

35:40.000 --> 35:41.320
I was,

35:42.440 --> 35:43.680
but I'm not any more.

35:47.920 --> 35:49.880
You're not armed, Grace, are you?

35:49.960 --> 35:51.360
No, I'm not armed.

35:52.920 --> 35:54.320
I don't carry guns.

35:55.080 --> 35:56.400
I don't have to.

36:01.680 --> 36:04.480
You don't have a sense of humor
any more either.

36:04.560 --> 36:06.160
What are you talking about?

36:16.080 --> 36:19.360
Thing is, I hate reunions.

36:19.440 --> 36:22.520
I didn't want to sit here,
talking about nothing

36:22.600 --> 36:25.280
and dancing around
what we really want to say.

36:26.000 --> 36:27.200
So, now...

36:28.520 --> 36:33.120
I know you're happy in New York, your
husband's rich and sweet and kind to you.

36:33.200 --> 36:34.640
I know you're unarmed.

36:34.720 --> 36:36.640
And you didn't come
here for sex,

36:36.720 --> 36:38.760
because you don't love
me any more.

36:39.560 --> 36:41.520
And it's only three minutes past.

36:43.560 --> 36:44.720
Another drink.

36:48.480 --> 36:50.160
I'll take that as a yes.

36:52.240 --> 36:54.040
[sighs]

36:54.120 --> 36:55.800
It's good to see you, Grace.

36:57.640 --> 36:59.360
So you didn't light the fire?

37:03.800 --> 37:05.680
You see, my real plan...

37:07.840 --> 37:09.560
Was that we go out.

37:11.240 --> 37:12.880
I want to impress you.

37:13.760 --> 37:15.000
Now...

37:17.120 --> 37:18.840
Do you like Charlie Chaplin?

37:21.240 --> 37:22.920
Yes, I like Charlie Chaplin.

37:23.200 --> 37:24.200
Good.

37:25.400 --> 37:28.360
But I bet you've never heard
Charlie Chaplin speak.

37:28.440 --> 37:30.240
[jazz music playing]

37:30.320 --> 37:32.880
Aren't you taking me to see
Charlie Chaplin.

37:32.960 --> 37:34.120
I am.

37:34.200 --> 37:37.760
- This isn't a picture house.
- No, it's not a picture house.

37:37.840 --> 37:39.960
So, how will I see Charlie Chaplin?

37:40.040 --> 37:43.560
You will see him and you will hear him
just like I promised.

37:43.640 --> 37:45.400
There you go, there's Chaplin.

37:45.480 --> 37:47.000
Oh, my God, that's him.

37:47.080 --> 37:49.640
That's really Charlie Chaplin in person.

37:49.720 --> 37:51.840
And in England announcing his film.

37:51.920 --> 37:54.520
And how the hell
do you know Charlie Chaplin?

37:54.600 --> 37:57.240
I don't. I know his bodyguard,
Wag MacDonald.

37:57.400 --> 37:58.720
It's that chap there.

37:58.840 --> 38:02.520
Wag was a bookie in Birmingham
and then he went to Los Angeles.

38:02.640 --> 38:05.120
Wag is also a Romany Gypsy, as is Chaplin,

38:05.200 --> 38:06.920
but he keeps it a secret.

38:07.000 --> 38:09.040
Chaplin was born
on the Black Patch,

38:09.120 --> 38:10.720
a Gypsy camp in Birmingham.

38:10.800 --> 38:14.080
That's why he gave Wag the job
though he was on the run.

38:14.160 --> 38:15.280
Thank you.

38:17.520 --> 38:18.520
Thank you.

38:18.600 --> 38:21.040
See, we all have our secrets, Grace.

38:21.120 --> 38:22.800
Come on, I'll introduce you.

38:26.480 --> 38:30.080
Hello, Wag, Mr. Chaplin,
this is Grace.

38:30.160 --> 38:31.840
[Grace] Hello, Mr. Chaplin.

38:34.520 --> 38:36.800
[phone ringing]

38:39.920 --> 38:42.360
- Hello.
- [Thomas] Hello, Mr. Campbell.

38:42.440 --> 38:46.280
You said you knew my sister's address
in Primrose Hill.

38:46.360 --> 38:50.440
So I expect you have men watching
the house to see who comes and goes.

38:50.880 --> 38:55.400
Tonight your men will see me return
to the house with a very beautiful woman.

38:55.480 --> 38:58.600
She will stay
until just before midnight.

38:59.000 --> 39:01.200
Of course, I'll close the curtains.

39:02.280 --> 39:04.120
Can you guess who the woman is?

39:07.080 --> 39:08.280
Liar!

39:08.360 --> 39:10.240
Sleep well, Mr. Campbell.

39:20.040 --> 39:21.200
[whispering] Tommy.

39:23.200 --> 39:25.040
Tommy, do you have someone?

39:33.200 --> 39:34.800
It's too late, Tommy.

39:36.000 --> 39:37.520
It's 11:00, Grace.

39:37.600 --> 39:39.320
I mean, it's too late.

39:42.240 --> 39:44.360
If you'd come with me
to New York...

39:45.200 --> 39:46.640
I had things to do.

39:49.360 --> 39:51.600
You mean the coin landed
the wrong way?

39:53.080 --> 39:54.800
It couldn't have worked.

39:56.720 --> 39:58.320
What was the question?

40:11.080 --> 40:13.160
Tommy, do you have someone?

40:13.240 --> 40:15.600
[takes a deep breath]

40:16.680 --> 40:18.120
I have a racehorse.

40:19.600 --> 40:21.200
She's gonna win the Derby.

40:24.000 --> 40:28.120
[song playing]

41:15.800 --> 41:16.920
I'll drive you.

41:17.000 --> 41:18.560
[clears throat]

41:22.680 --> 41:24.040
When do you sail back?

41:26.920 --> 41:28.040
We don't know yet.

41:29.880 --> 41:31.720
You don't have a return ticket?

41:32.880 --> 41:34.520
This wasn't right, Tommy.

41:36.120 --> 41:37.840
Then you go back, Grace.

41:43.240 --> 41:44.760
They're doing tests on us.

41:45.240 --> 41:47.520
I don't know when they'll be finished.

41:51.920 --> 41:53.320
We're having treatment.

41:54.520 --> 41:56.280
A doctor in Harley Street.

41:57.360 --> 41:59.280
Some new thing, a breakthrough.

42:02.680 --> 42:04.480
We're trying for a baby.

42:19.080 --> 42:20.400
[inhales sharply]

42:28.960 --> 42:30.720
Why did you come here tonight?

42:37.480 --> 42:40.400
The Doctor believes it's surely
me who's at fault.

42:43.160 --> 42:44.440
I'm sorry.

42:48.240 --> 42:51.440
- It's no one's fault.
- I'm tired of that, Tommy.

43:02.880 --> 43:04.520
Can I see you again?

43:08.840 --> 43:10.120
Grace.

43:15.320 --> 43:17.480
You're still working undercover, eh?

43:20.080 --> 43:21.840
I have never lied to him once.

43:24.840 --> 43:26.360
So tell him the truth.

43:45.880 --> 43:47.440
Put your arms up.

43:56.320 --> 43:58.000
What have we got here then?

43:58.440 --> 43:59.960
[door opens]

44:02.600 --> 44:04.480
Take your fucking hands off me!

44:06.120 --> 44:07.600
Here he is.

44:07.680 --> 44:09.360
The king of London town.

44:19.480 --> 44:22.480
- You been enjoying yourself?
- Yes, fucking great.

44:23.160 --> 44:25.120
Surrounded by Sabini's men.

44:25.600 --> 44:26.920
Rats everywhere.

44:27.840 --> 44:30.160
- Fucking cockneys.
- [snorts]

44:30.280 --> 44:33.480
At least you're going to get
what you've always wanted.

44:33.560 --> 44:36.400
- What?
- Well, you tried to hang yourself twice.

44:36.680 --> 44:38.880
Now, the King is gonna
do it for you.

44:38.960 --> 44:40.080
[chuckles]

44:42.600 --> 44:44.200
I've been a fucking idiot.

44:44.280 --> 44:45.360
Yeah.

44:46.760 --> 44:48.960
I haven't appreciated nothing, John.

44:49.040 --> 44:52.040
- Are you fucking repenting or something?
- Drawing.

44:52.520 --> 44:54.240
I used to be good at drawing.

44:54.320 --> 44:56.400
Arthur, please. I don't need this--

44:56.480 --> 44:58.560
I should've listened more in class.

44:58.640 --> 45:01.040
What fucking class?
You were never there.

45:01.840 --> 45:04.080
I used to draw horses.

45:04.160 --> 45:06.320
- Arthur--
- Stallions.

45:06.400 --> 45:08.080
- Great, big ones.
- Arthur.

45:08.160 --> 45:10.800
- They looked real--
- Not stallions, not now.

45:11.280 --> 45:13.960
I should've done more
with my life, John.

45:14.120 --> 45:15.560
- Good things.
- Arthur--

45:15.640 --> 45:19.280
- Even Ada said it wasn't my fault.
- Arthur, will you listen?

45:19.360 --> 45:21.720
- They're gonna hang me.
- They will not.

45:21.880 --> 45:23.200
Says who?

45:25.160 --> 45:26.360
Tommy.

45:30.200 --> 45:32.960
And how is Houdini going to
get me out of this?

45:33.040 --> 45:35.800
- Well--
- Don't tell me. He's got a plan.

45:35.880 --> 45:38.360
But you don't know that plan,
do you, John?

45:38.440 --> 45:40.000
- 'Cause we just--
- I do--

45:40.080 --> 45:41.760
We can't be trusted.

45:41.840 --> 45:43.040
All right,

45:43.120 --> 45:45.280
if he's so fucking clever,

45:45.360 --> 45:47.040
- why am I in here?
- Well--

45:47.120 --> 45:50.160
Why is all our men and half
our whiskey being lifted?

45:50.240 --> 45:51.320
Mm?

45:51.400 --> 45:54.280
The Jew and the cockney
have run rings round him.

45:54.360 --> 45:56.680
- Will you shut up?
- Look at you, look.

45:56.760 --> 45:59.600
- A big fucking man--
- [loudly] Fucking shut up!

46:02.080 --> 46:04.480
He's already told me
what I've got to do.

46:07.440 --> 46:09.800
[car approaching]

46:22.360 --> 46:24.520
What business have you got here?

46:24.600 --> 46:25.960
I've just pulled over.

46:26.040 --> 46:28.320
I never smoke and drive, you know?

46:28.400 --> 46:31.120
- Where are you from?
- I'm from Ireland.

46:31.200 --> 46:33.960
North where the rocks sing in the wind.

46:34.040 --> 46:36.280
[officer]
Where in the beautiful north?

46:36.360 --> 46:39.800
- I just pull over for--
- I wanna see some identification.

46:49.920 --> 46:51.680
[loud explosion]

46:58.200 --> 47:00.440
[song playing]

47:07.400 --> 47:09.480
[birds chirping]

47:21.000 --> 47:22.520
Look.

47:22.600 --> 47:24.120
Come.

47:27.320 --> 47:28.560
See?

47:32.800 --> 47:35.680
Does it really stop the horses
from getting worms?

47:36.440 --> 47:38.200
Yep, it really does.

47:43.680 --> 47:45.880
Anyway, I thought
it'd make you smile.

47:46.680 --> 47:50.720
I'm sorry that you had to drive through
the night, must be exhausted.

47:50.800 --> 47:52.800
You can go and sleep if you want.

47:54.320 --> 47:55.400
May.

47:57.480 --> 47:58.560
We have to stop...

47:59.720 --> 48:00.920
This.

48:02.360 --> 48:04.520
Came here to tell you
we have to stop.

48:07.200 --> 48:08.280
Why?

48:09.440 --> 48:11.920
That I'm me and you're you?
That old thing?

48:13.160 --> 48:14.240
There's someone.

48:17.280 --> 48:18.840
For a long time.

48:23.640 --> 48:25.880
And I didn't want you to
think anything

48:25.960 --> 48:28.200
about how it's gonna be
after the race.

48:29.560 --> 48:30.800
[clears throat]

48:32.520 --> 48:34.680
Not many of your people
know about me,

48:34.760 --> 48:37.400
so I haven't done the damage
that would come.

48:37.480 --> 48:38.680
"My people"?

48:41.480 --> 48:44.800
But the damage isn't done,
is what I mean.

48:44.880 --> 48:46.040
Right.

48:48.880 --> 48:52.000
Even if it's like this,
I want the horse to stay here.

48:52.120 --> 48:53.880
To stay, yes, of course.

48:53.960 --> 48:55.160
Epsom is close--

48:55.240 --> 48:58.000
I haven't got my outfit yet,
so it's all right.

48:58.440 --> 49:00.880
You can still be with me
in the enclosure.

49:00.960 --> 49:02.880
That's very gracious
of you, sir.

49:03.240 --> 49:06.160
- You can wear something--
- It's funny, isn't it?

49:06.240 --> 49:09.480
Because you'll be up there
and I'll be down in the ring.

49:09.560 --> 49:11.360
Sort of upside down, isn't it?

49:12.080 --> 49:15.120
You can be with me after
and still wear something--

49:15.200 --> 49:17.360
I'll be covered in mud
from the ring.

49:20.000 --> 49:21.840
May, forget about men like me--

49:21.920 --> 49:24.720
I was going to tell you
how much she's improved.

49:29.760 --> 49:31.440
There are other men, May--

49:31.520 --> 49:34.040
I think she stands a chance
at placing, sir.

49:34.120 --> 49:36.440
The silly part of our business is done.

49:36.520 --> 49:39.760
Are you going to drive straight off
to Birmingham, or...

49:43.520 --> 49:45.320
And what if I said, uh,

49:45.960 --> 49:47.360
"All right, I'll stay."

49:47.680 --> 49:49.240
After what I just said?

49:55.360 --> 49:57.080
Then that would be all right.

50:02.880 --> 50:05.760
You talk about damage,
the damage not yet done.

50:05.840 --> 50:07.840
You don't think
that half of London

50:07.920 --> 50:10.480
already thinks that
I'm fucking a racketeer?

50:10.560 --> 50:14.600
Laughing about it, laying on bets about
when you'll steal the silver?

50:15.920 --> 50:18.520
You think your people
are ruthless? Try mine.

50:22.520 --> 50:24.760
So that's why you'd carry on, eh?

50:25.400 --> 50:27.280
Because you can't back down.

50:29.080 --> 50:31.880
Amongst many other illogical reasons.

50:36.040 --> 50:38.160
So will you drive straight off or...

50:38.240 --> 50:40.520
I haven't got any petrol
in the garage.

50:44.200 --> 50:46.760
Yeah, I have some
cans of petrol in the car.

50:46.840 --> 50:48.040
Good, so you can go.

50:56.440 --> 50:57.880
[clears throat]

51:12.160 --> 51:13.360
[sniffs]

51:17.600 --> 51:19.360
They look happy in there, eh?

51:21.200 --> 51:22.840
And why wouldn't they be?

51:36.000 --> 51:37.160
Who is she?

51:39.560 --> 51:41.440
Someone who's sailing away.

51:50.800 --> 51:52.200
So let her sail.

51:55.160 --> 51:57.600
You've told me about her
like a gentleman,

51:57.680 --> 52:00.000
now kindly behave
like a gangster again.

52:04.880 --> 52:06.560
Feel sorry for me, it's fine.

52:17.240 --> 52:19.920
Because your horse
will come fifth or sixth...

52:21.440 --> 52:23.120
But I will win you.

52:31.200 --> 52:33.160
Mr. Shelby's just
parking his car,

52:33.240 --> 52:35.120
he said for you
to wait in here.

52:40.160 --> 52:41.840
Isn't this impressive?

52:43.080 --> 52:45.800
And what is it you exactly do here?

52:47.320 --> 52:50.560
I exactly am a secretary
to Mr. Shelby.

52:50.640 --> 52:53.280
A secretary! My, my, my.

52:54.240 --> 52:56.120
All that paperwork.

52:58.120 --> 52:59.160
Do you want tea?

53:00.120 --> 53:01.280
No.

53:39.560 --> 53:40.760
[door closes]

53:47.000 --> 53:49.440
I keep everything locked up,
Mr. Campbell.

53:49.520 --> 53:51.000
Everything of value.

53:51.880 --> 53:53.160
[clears throat]

53:59.520 --> 54:00.920
Take a seat.

54:01.000 --> 54:02.240
[clears throat]

54:05.800 --> 54:08.560
How is your company
treasurer, Polly?

54:10.640 --> 54:12.160
Why do you ask?

54:12.240 --> 54:14.800
Just give her my regards.

54:18.360 --> 54:19.600
[sighs]

54:25.440 --> 54:27.800
You like to play with fire.

54:28.520 --> 54:30.000
Don't you, Mr. Shelby?

54:31.640 --> 54:35.320
Yesterday, in Belgravia,

54:35.520 --> 54:38.520
Field Marshal Russell's house
was burned out.

54:38.600 --> 54:42.520
An incendiary device was put through
his letter box, which means...

54:43.920 --> 54:46.680
That he will have to find
somewhere else to live

54:46.760 --> 54:48.840
for at least the next
three months.

54:48.920 --> 54:49.840
Hmm.

54:50.720 --> 54:53.240
Which also means that your plan

54:53.320 --> 54:55.800
for me to break in
and shoot him in his bed

54:55.880 --> 54:58.200
is no longer
an operational possibility.

54:58.280 --> 54:59.400
Indeed.

54:59.480 --> 55:04.280
But if you think a wee burn frees you from
your obligations, think again--

55:04.360 --> 55:07.480
- I will keep my side of the bargain.
- Oh, you will.

55:07.560 --> 55:09.440
I will shoot
your Field Marshal,

55:09.520 --> 55:12.200
but I will do in a way
that serves my purpose.

55:12.280 --> 55:14.200
The only purpose is my purpose.

55:14.280 --> 55:17.880
I will carry out your assassination
at a place of my choosing.

55:19.280 --> 55:20.640
Listen to me.

55:21.480 --> 55:24.440
All operational detail
must be mutually agreed--

55:24.520 --> 55:27.720
I'm a soldier, I can determine
where and when--

55:27.800 --> 55:30.520
That man has 24-hour
armed police protection--

55:30.600 --> 55:33.120
Your plan was full of holes,
Mr. Campbell--

55:33.200 --> 55:35.080
My plan was mutually agreed--

55:35.160 --> 55:36.960
Now your plan is up in smoke!

55:37.040 --> 55:39.840
And I've formulated
the only viable alternative.

55:40.280 --> 55:42.200
For God's sake,
what do you mean?

55:43.240 --> 55:44.760
How would you get to him?

55:47.480 --> 55:48.520
I won't.

55:49.120 --> 55:50.400
He will come to me.

55:54.520 --> 55:56.400
Now, listen to me, Mr. Shelby.

55:56.720 --> 55:58.560
When this meeting is concluded,

55:58.840 --> 56:00.720
I must report directly

56:00.800 --> 56:02.720
to Mr. Winston Churchill.

56:02.800 --> 56:05.160
Your relationship with Mr. Churchill

56:05.240 --> 56:06.600
is not my concern.

56:07.240 --> 56:09.120
And Mr. Winston Churchill

56:09.200 --> 56:11.640
will need to hear detail.

56:11.720 --> 56:14.200
Well, you tell him
he'll have to trust me.

56:18.160 --> 56:20.400
Look, Mr. Campbell...
[clears throat]

56:20.760 --> 56:22.880
I will carry out my mission.

56:23.400 --> 56:25.320
- Good.
- Good.

56:25.720 --> 56:27.320
But I will do it in a place

56:27.400 --> 56:30.480
where it will be impossible
for you or your men

56:30.560 --> 56:32.680
to have me shot afterwards.

56:34.440 --> 56:36.400
Because that was the plan.

56:36.760 --> 56:37.960
Eh?

56:38.120 --> 56:40.480
Coppers front and back,
no way out.

56:40.560 --> 56:42.920
Me shot dead,
dumped in the Thames.

56:43.000 --> 56:44.280
I will do the killing

56:44.960 --> 56:47.760
but in a place where
that will not be an option.

56:49.760 --> 56:53.760
[clears throat] I've recently become
a racehorse owner, Mr. Campbell.

56:57.240 --> 56:58.320
Oh.

56:58.400 --> 56:59.800
It's, uh...

57:01.400 --> 57:04.960
Well, perhaps you can guess
which one is my horse. [coughs]

57:22.000 --> 57:23.600
Where and when?

57:26.240 --> 57:27.360
Epsom.

57:28.480 --> 57:29.720
Derby day.

57:30.880 --> 57:33.800
[theme song playing]
